              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for the brake, then the German for to change gear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: der Scheinwerfer",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "der Scheinwerfer — \"the headlight; the spotlight\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Am Abend schaltet sie die Scheinwerfer ein. In the evening she switches the headlights on."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Same form in the plural: die Scheinwerfer. On a stage, the spotlight is also der Scheinwerfer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Scheinwerfer is built from Schein 'light, glow' and Werfer 'thrower', from werfen 'to throw': a thrower of light. Both are inherited: Schein goes back to Proto-Germanic skīnaną 'to shine' and werfen to werpaną 'to throw' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
